<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.10.4: Matching Inequalities and Solutions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00549</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.10.4: Matching Inequalities and Solutions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>63a88e79-804c-4b66-9773-65a8a3014c54</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Match each inequality to a graph that represents its solutions. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
<list>
  <item>\(6x\;\leq\;3x\)</item>
  <item>\(\frac14x&gt;-\frac12\)</item>
  <item>\(5x+4\geq7x\)</item>
  <item>\(8x-2&lt;-4(x-1)\)</item>
  <item>\(\frac{4x-1}3&gt;-1\)</item>
  <item>\(\frac{12}5-\frac x5\leq x\)</item>
</list>
<para>Graph A</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At negative one half, open circle with line extending to the right.  "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2d621974e0882d1c29a952d999cd031e4b1acd5a"/></media></figure><para>Graph B</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At two, closed circle with line extending to the left.  "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5c1504f5073145ae656f9e928daa3f6a8b289e7c"/></media></figure><para>Graph C</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At two, closed circle with line extending to the right."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e96d18ea04eb10c86b9797284fff1c676aa8c022"/></media></figure><para>Graph D</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At  one half, open circle with line extending to the left.  "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e9b8072106740850d58157b4ee2d9e36e056e931"/></media></figure><para>Graph E</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At negative 2, open circle with line extending to the right."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3afda547f9abbeb3d436ab4a16f63d661fc76af9"/></media></figure><para>Graph F</para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a number line. Numbers from negative 10 to 10. At 0, closed circle with line extending to the left."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/099eae57745932eb4032ebbc413163b4adb69884"/></media></figure><para>Use this inequality for questions 1 - 2:</para>
<para><quote>\(6x\le3x\)</quote></para><!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="04f58b3f-9635-4c5e-b81d-558a3314c7bc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Match the graph to the equation.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Graph F.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is Graph F.</para></solution></exercise></section><!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
